      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">When a two‑wheeler or motorcycle arrives at its destination, the handover process is designed to confirm that the vehicle’s condition and mileage match the records captured at pickup.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The delivery team follows a strict, three‑step protocol: daylight re‑inspection against the original pickup photographs, odometer verification against the LR bilty, and a signed condition sign‑off by the recipient.</span></li></ul>

<div style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.08); border-left: 4px solid #f59e0b; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 18px 22px; margin: 24px 0;"><h4 style="color: #f59e0b; font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle" style="margin-right: 8px;"></i>Important Logistics Advisory</h4><div style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.92rem; margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">The daylight re‑inspection begins immediately upon arrival. The delivery rider or dispatcher pulls out the high‑resolution images taken during the pickup and compares each angle—front, rear, side, undercarriage, and interior—to the vehicle on the road.</p>
<p>Any scratches, dents, or fluid leaks that were not documented at pickup trigger a corrective action request. The team marks the photo set with a “verified” stamp and records any discrepancies in the handover log.</p>

<p>Odometer verification is the next critical step. The rider reads the mileage on the motorcycle’s odometer and cross‑checks it with the figure listed on the LR bilty.</p>
<p>A difference of more than five kilometres is flagged for investigation, and the rider must capture a fresh photo of the odometer display to attach to the delivery report. This ensures that mileage fraud is detected before the vehicle leaves the delivery hub.</div></div>

<p>Finally, the recipient signs a condition sign‑off form that mirrors the pickup checklist. The form lists key inspection points—tire tread, brake function, headlight operation, and overall bodywork.</p>
<p>By signing, the recipient acknowledges that the motorcycle matches the documented condition and mileage, and that any noted issues are either pre‑existing or have been resolved. The signed form is scanned, appended to the digital delivery package, and stored in the fleet management system for audit purposes.</p>

